 "description": "Every place that shows the LynkOmni brand and which asset it uses. `choose` lists the assets in order of preference; the first whose minWidthPx fits the space available is used, and the last entry has no minimum. `colour` is 'theme' (follows the user's theme) or 'mono' (one colour). A 'live' surface must resolve against the vendored brand; a 'planned' surface is a promise that, when built, it will ask the brand module for its surface id and never name a file or a colour.",
